abstract: >-
  A multi-country, multi-model benchmark quantifying geographic bias in
  Large Language Models when used for applied research on public policy,
  socioeconomic reality, and environmental context in the Global South.
  The analysis plan was fixed before data collection but never deposited
  publicly, so the study claims no pre-registration and is reported as
  exploratory. Covers 25 countries (stratified via UNCTAD, Joshi et
  al. 2020, World Bank classifications), 14 LLMs (frontier proprietary,
  open-source global, regional), and a sparse factorial matrix of prompt
  languages. All prompts, ground-truth references, code, and responses
  will be released on publication under CC-BY-4.0 (data, prompts, documentation)
  and MIT (code). Until then this repository carries the protocol, the analysis
  code and the manuscript; the per-response records live outside the public tree.
